The '''PYRAMID30 Okaiken''' is a chart that ranks the best-performing singles in [[Okaiken]]. Its data, published by Nikkan Sports & Entertainment magazine, KTK Group and compiled by Okaiken Pyramid Records, is based collectively on each single's weekly physical and digital sales, as well as radio airplay and streaming. PYRAMID30 Okaiken is a subsidiary of Pyramid Records but acts as a separate organization. The weekly charts are updated every Sunday at 11:45 in the morning (UTC +9). The following lists all of the number one singles of the PYRAMID30 Okaiken for 2021.

2021 is known in Okaiken music history as the "Year of Noise" ({{nihongo|Zatsu-on no Toshi|雑音の年}}). Following the quiet introspection of the 2020 pandemic era, the Sanese public craved chaotic, high-energy aggression. While [[Ado (singer)|Ado]]'s "Usseewa" set the tone early in the year, the charts were defined by the unexpected viral explosion of the Kyoto punk band [[Otoboke Beaver]]. Their track "Pardon?" became a social media phenomenon, introducing "Okaiken Punk" to a mainstream audience for the first time in decades. The year also saw the early seeds of the "Drill" movement with rapper [[Ralph (rapper)|Ralph]] claiming his first number one.

